```=html
<aside>Also known as a <a href="https://indieweb.org/colophon" target="_blank" rel="noopener">colophon</a> or <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Style_guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">style guide</a>.</aside>
```

Built with my own [static site generator](https://github.com/iamseeley/tseeley.com), written in Rust. It uses [jotdown](https://crates.io/crates/jotdown) for content, [maud](https://crates.io/crates/maud) for templates, and [axum](https://crates.io/crates/axum) for the dev server. Served by [Caddy](https://caddyserver.com/) on a [Hetzner](https://www.hetzner.com/) VPS.

## Design

Designed and built by me. Everything is intentionally simple: plain HTML, CSS, and minimal JavaScript. Much of the design inspiration comes from the sites in my [blogroll](/blogroll/).

### Mascot

The site's mascot is Sally, a [Blue Ridge Gray-cheeked Salamander](https://auth1.dpr.ncparks.gov/amphibians/view.php?sciName=Plethodon+amplus) (_Plethodon amplus_). She's native to the Southern Appalachian mountains of North Carolina. You'll spot her around the site.

### Typography

Headers are set in [Georgia](<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georgia_(typeface)>) and body copy is set in [Verdana](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdana).

### Links

Links are styled to indicate their destination:

- **Internal links** have solid underlines, like [this link to posts](/posts/)
- **External links** have dashed underlines, like [this link to djot](https://djot.net/)

### Code

Inline code like `fn main()` and code blocks are set in [Lilex](https://github.com/mishamyrt/Lilex). Code blocks show a language label in the top right corner.

```rust
fn main() {
    println!("Language labels use the code font.");
}
```

### Dinkus

Section breaks use a centered dinkus (three spaced asterisks).

---

Like that.

### Feeds

The main [posts feed](/atom.xml) includes the full post content. Each [tag page](/tags/) also has its own feed.

### Layout

Single column on small screens. On wider viewports the nav moves to a sidebar column on the right. The content area is capped at 640px.

### Elements

The site uses a few recurring content patterns. Since djot doesn't pass raw HTML through by default, these are written as `` ```=html `` blocks.

**Aside**: a callout with a left border, same style as blockquotes.

```=html
<aside>This is what an aside looks like.</aside>
```

**Blockquote**: a styled quote with attribution.

```=html
<blockquote>
    <q>The computer is the first metamedium, and as such it has degrees of freedom for representation and expression never before encountered.</q>
    <cite>Alan Kay</cite>
</blockquote>
```

**Figure**: an image with a caption.

```=html
<figure style="max-width: 200px">
  <img src="/images/cute-ferris.png" alt="Cute Ferris the crab">
  <figcaption>Ferris by <a href="https://rustacean.net/">Karen Rustad Tölva</a>, CC0.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

## AI

I write everything here myself. The ideas, opinions, and structure are mine.

I use AI tools for research, but I do the drafting and editing myself.

I don't publish anything I haven't read, edited, and stand behind. If my practice changes significantly, I'll update this page.

## Privacy

This site doesn't use cookies, doesn't track you across the web, and doesn't collect personal data.

I use [Umami](https://umami.is/) for basic, privacy-respecting analytics (page views, referrers). It's self-hosted, collects no personal information, and is fully compliant with [GDPR](https://gdpr-info.eu/), [CCPA](https://oag.ca.gov/privacy/ccpa), and [PECR](https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/direct-marketing-and-privacy-and-electronic-communications/guide-to-pecr/what-are-pecr/) without requiring a cookie banner.
